.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt VFS_LANTEST 1
.Os Netatalk Client
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_lantest
.Nd File operation latency benchmark for a mounted filesystem
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cDK
.Op Fl f Ar tests
.Op Fl n Ar iterations
.Op Fl q Ar KiB
.Op Fl s Ar MiB
.Fl P Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the test set of the Netatalk server benchmark
.Xr afp_lantest 1
as POSIX file operations in
.Ar directory ,
so that a mounted filesystem is measured end to end: the kernel, the
filesystem client and the server behind it.
On a FUSE mount of an AFP volume that is the Netatalk client; on a CIFS
mount it is the kernel SMB client; on a local directory it is the
filesystem alone.
The seventeen tests, their order, their 2000-item geometry, the
statistics and the CSV layout are those of
.Xr afp_lantest 1 ,
so the same chart and history scripts read both.
.Pp
Every data read and write opens with
.Dv O_DIRECT ,
so the kernel page cache never answers for the filesystem behind the mount.
A plain local filesystem refuses
.Dv O_DIRECT
for the 1024-byte transfers of the small-file tests; pass
.Fl D
there.
.Pp
Server-side copies are issued with
.Xr copy_file_range 2 :
an SMB3 or NFS 4.2 server, or a FUSE daemon implementing the operation,
copies without the data crossing the mount; otherwise the kernel moves it.
.Pp
Results go to standard output, progress and diagnostics to standard error.
The tests run in a directory named
.Pa LanTest- Ns Aq Ar pid
under
.Ar directory ,
which is removed at the end.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl P Ar directory
Directory on the mounted filesystem to run in.
.It Fl c
CSV output: one row per test with the mean, standard deviation, minimum,
maximum and median in milliseconds and the MB/s of the large-file tests,
then the sum row and the aggregate block.
.It Fl D
Buffered I/O in place of
.Dv O_DIRECT .
.It Fl f Ar tests
Comma-separated test numbers, 1 to 17 (default: all).
The tests that use the shared 2000 files pull in their creation and
deletion.
.It Fl K
The four cache-focused tests only (14 to 17).
.It Fl n Ar iterations
Passes over the test set, 1 to 1000 (default: 2).
Above five, the fastest and slowest sample of every test are dropped.
.It Fl q Ar KiB
Chunk size of the large-file tests (default: 1024).
.It Fl s Ar MiB
Size of the large file (default: 100); a multiple of the chunk size.
.El
.Sh TESTS
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Writing one large file, one write per chunk and the close
.It
Reading it back, one read per chunk and the close
.It
Creating 2000 files with
.Xr mknod 2
and a stat of each
.It
Creating a 20x9x10 directory tree
.It
Open, write 1024 bytes, close, for each of the 2000 files
.It
Open, read 1024 bytes, close, for each
.It
Copying 1000 files through user space
.It
Copying 2000 files with
.Xr copy_file_range 2
.It
Stat of each file
.It
Listing the directory and stat of every entry
.It
Lock then unlock one byte in each of the 2000 open files
.It
Deleting the 2000 files
.It
Lock then unlock 2000 byte ranges of one file
.It
Stat of 20 directories and their 100 files each
.It
Create, stat, stat, delete on 500 files, listing every tenth round
.It
100 walks of a 20-level directory chain, one stat per level
.It
Four stats of each of 500 files
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A failed file operation exits with status 2 after removing what the run
created; a usage error exits with status 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Twenty passes over a FUSE mount, as CSV:
.Pp
.Dl $ vfs_lantest -c -n 20 -P /mnt/afpfs > lantest.csv
.Pp
A quick run on a local directory with a 4 MiB large file:
.Pp
.Dl $ vfs_lantest -D -n 2 -s 4 -P /tmp/scratch
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr afp_lantest 1 ,
.Xr mount_afpfs 1 ,
.Xr vfs_speedtest 1
